view another driver's routes.\",\n      \"kind\": \"permission\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"For each route, show its stops and the boxes expected at each stop. During the route, show each box's latest available temperature, status and alerts; when readings are unavailable or stale, make that visible.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Before departure, the driver scans each box being loaded. Accept scans for expected route boxes, identify boxes assigned to another route, and report expected boxes not scanned. Do not mark loading complete until every expected route box has been scanned and no wrong box is treated as loaded.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"If a scanned box is not on the route, identify it as a wrong-route box and prevent it from satisfying an expected-box scan. If any expected box is missing, show which box is missing and keep loading incomplete.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"At a stop, the driver scans boxes expected for that stop and sees whether each can be handed over. For a box with On Hold stock, show “Do not deliver” and the hold reason, and prevent that box from being handed over.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"For eligible boxes, let the driver record the receiver's name, capture a signature and a photo of delivered boxes, and complete the handover. Record handover time and location automatically.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Allow the driver to record refusal of all or selected boxes, capturing a reason for each refused box. Record refused boxes as returning to the warehouse and set them to Quarantined when they arrive.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Allow loading, handover and refusal to be recorded while disconnected, retain the work locally until connectivity returns, and send it automatically when connectivity returns. Preserve the time the offline handover actually occurred rather than substituting its upload time.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"If the route changed while the driver was offline, show the driver the differences before they continue, including affected stops or boxes. Do not discard or undo a handover already completed offline when reconciling the route.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"If an offline handover is uploaded after a hold was placed on that box, keep the handover, flag the hold/handover conflict and open a quality case; do not silently reject or erase the handover.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"If the same handover is submitted more than once, retain one recorded handover rather than creating duplicates.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Show dispatchers the status of each stop and the time it was last updated.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"readingChosen\": \"Treat driver workflows as features of the responsive web app, including browser-based offline use; when disconnected, show the latest available box temperature/status and identify it as potentially stale rather than implying a live reading.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"US-010: Decide What Happens to Affected Stock\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"For every affected handling unit, require a recorded decision of Release or Reject. Show the reviewer the full temperature history, budget used and remaining for every tier, and the system recommendation: Release if every tier has allowance remaining; Reject if any tier is exhausted or a not-permitted range was reached.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Allow a Quality Officer to make and sign a decision alone only when the excursion stayed within the first tier above or below the band and allowance remains.\",\n      \"kind\": \"permission\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"For every other case, require a Quality Officer to propose and a different person acting as Quality Manager to approve. Do not allow the proposer to approve, even if that person holds both roles.\",\n      \"kind\": \"permission\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"If the proposed decision goes against the system recommendation, require both Quality Officer proposal and Quality Manager approval and require a written justification.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"At signing, require the decision-maker to confirm their identity again and enter a reason. Record each decision as electronically signed.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"After signing, prevent anyone, including a System Administrator, from editing or deleting the decision. Permit a later decision only as a new signed decision that supersedes the earlier one, retaining both in the record.\",\n      \"kind\": \"permission\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Keep On Hold stock unavailable for allocation, packing, loading and handover.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"On Release, restore the stock to its prior disposition: available stock remains available, and stock previously on an order or route returns to that order or route.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"On Reject, remove the stock from its order and trigger reallocation of the order under US-005; remove rejected stock from available stock and list it for destruction.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Allow destruction to be recorded with a date, quantity and witness, and reject any destruction entry that would make the destroyed quantity exceed the rejected quantity.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Escalate a decision that has been waiting longer than four hours to the Quality Manager.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     }\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"US-011: Recall a Lot\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Allow only a Quality Manager to start a recall, specifying a product, one or more lot numbers, a reason and severity; record the start as signed. Allow only a Quality Manager to close a recall, also as a signed action.\",\n      \"kind\": \"permission\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"On starting a recall, set all Meridian-held stock in the specified lots, across all warehouses, to Recalled and block it from allocation/use and handover, including stock already packed or on a vehicle.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"When a route device is online, show “Do not deliver” for a recalled box. Apply the block to the recalled box even if it is already on a route.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Make a trace available within one minute showing every affected warehouse location, box, route and customer delivery, with quantities, and list customers who received the lots with quantities, delivery dates and receivers. Ensure trace quantities reconcile exactly to the lot's total quantity received.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Notify affected customers by email and in the customer portal. Let each customer respond in the portal for each delivery with packs still on hand, used or dispensed, and destroyed on site.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Reject a customer response whose reported quantities exceed the quantity delivered to that customer for that delivery.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Arrange packs reported on hand for collection on a return route and set them to Quarantined when they arrive.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"After 24 hours without a customer response, send that customer a reminder and show the outstanding customer to the Quality Manager.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Show recall progress as the percentage of packs accounted for.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Allow recall closure only when every pack is accounted for as held by Meridian, returned, reported used, reported destroyed, or written off as unaccounted with a signed justification. Do not allow closure while any pack is unaccounted for without such a write-off.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     }\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"US-012: Follow Orders in the Customer Portal\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Show a customer user current and past orders belonging to that user's organisation only; prevent access to another organisation's orders.\",\n      \"kind\": \"permission\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"For orders, show status, allocated lots and expiry dates. For a delivery on the road, show planned arrival time and whether its temperature is in or out of range, without exposing other customers on the route.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"For each completed delivery, let the customer download a PDF delivery certificate containing products, lots, expiry dates, quantities, receiver and handover time, each box's temperature chart from sealing to handover, excursions and their signed decisions.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Keep an issued certificate version unchanged. If late readings change the history, issue a new certificate version and keep both the original and new versions available.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Show dates and times in the customer's own time zone, and provide the portal and certificates in English or Arabic according to the user's preference. When Arabic is selected, display the entire portal right-to-left, including tables and charts, and render the certificate accordingly.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     }\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"US-013: Audit Trail\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Record every creation, change and deletion of regulated data, including products and profiles, stock, orders and allocations, boxes and routes, handovers, excursions, decisions, recalls, users and roles, and configuration. Each entry records who acted, when, what changed, old and new values, and any reason provided.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Record automatic actions, such as automatic holds and allocations, with the system identified as the actor.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Prevent every user, including a System Administrator, from editing or deleting audit entries; provide evidence that can detect alteration of the trail outside the application.\",\n      \"kind\": \"permission\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Store audit times in one reference time and display them in the viewer's time zone, including the distinct time zones for Karachi/Lahore and Dubai. Retain records for seven years.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Let an Auditor filter the audit trail by record, user, date range and action type, and export any filtered view. Restrict this audit capability to an Auditor.\",\n      \"kind\": \"permission\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Let a user view the full history of one lot in time order, from receipt through delivery or destruction.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     }\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"US-014: Reports and Scheduled Summaries\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"At 07:00 in each warehouse's own time zone, email that warehouse's Quality Officers a daily summary of excursions in the last 24 hours, decisions still waiting, silent devices and stock On Hold.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"On the first day of each month, generate and email a monthly report to configured stakeholders. Include excursion count and rate by route, driver, vehicle and shipper-box type; packs rejected and destroyed by product and cause; on-time and in-full delivery percentages; average time from excursion to decision; stock expiring within 60 days by product and warehouse; and open recalls with progress.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Define on-time delivery as handover within 60 minutes of planned arrival, and in-full as handover of every ordered pack; calculate report figures from the underlying records for the same reporting period.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Let staff view the same figures on screen for any date range, filter by warehouse and export the report. Restrict each staff member's report figures to their own warehouses.\",\n      \"kind\": \"permission\"\n     }\n    ]\n   }\n  ]\n },\n {\n  \"spans\": [\n   {\n    \"id\": \"driver-route-loading-handover\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"A driver can view and act on only their own routes; attempts to open another driver's route are denied.\",\n      \"kind\": \"permission\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Before departure, the driver sees today's assigned route and its stops in order, with the route's boxes and loading status.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"When the driver scans a box for loading, the app identifies it and records the scan against the route.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"If a scanned box belongs to another route, the app identifies it as a wrong-route box and warns the driver; it is not counted as a valid route-box scan.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"The driver cannot complete loading or depart the route until every box assigned to the route has been scanned; the app identifies any missing boxes.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"During the route, the driver can see each box's current temperature, status, and alerts.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"At a stop, the driver scans the boxes assigned to that stop and sees which boxes are eligible for handover.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"If a box contains stock On Hold, the app displays “Do not deliver” and the hold reason and prevents the driver from recording its handover.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"For eligible boxes, the driver records the receiver's name, captures a signature and a photo of the delivered boxes, and completes handover.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"On handover, the app records the event time and location automatically, along with the receiver name, signature, photo, stop, and delivered boxes.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"The driver can record a refusal of all or part of a delivery, recording the refused boxes and a reason for each refused box; non-refused eligible boxes can still be handed over.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Refused boxes are recorded as returning to the warehouse and are marked Quarantined on arrival.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Loading, handover, and refusal can be recorded without a connection; the app retains the work locally and sends it automatically when connectivity returns.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"An offline handover retains the time it actually occurred, rather than being timestamped with its later upload time.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"If the server route changed while the driver was offline, the app shows the driver the differences before the driver continues with route work.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"A handover completed offline remains recorded if the route changed meanwhile; syncing the route change does not erase or undo that handover.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"If a box was put On Hold while the driver was offline but was handed over offline, the app retains the handover, flags the hold/handover conflict, and opens a quality case.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Sending the same handover more than once results in one recorded handover, not duplicate records.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"A dispatcher can see each stop's status and the time it was last updated.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"If location is unavailable or the driver does not grant browser location access, the app does not invent a location and indicates that it could not record one.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"readingChosen\": \"Treat the delivery workflow as one responsive web app; a refusal is recorded per affected box, and each refused box is returned to the warehouse and quarantined.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"US-010-affected-stock-decisions\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"For each affected handling unit, a reviewer sees the full temperature history, allowance used and remaining for each tier, and the system's Release or Reject recommendation.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"The system recommends Release only when every tier still has allowance; it recommends Reject if any tier's allowance is used up or a non-permitted range was reached.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"A Quality Officer can sign a decision alone only for an excursion confined to the first tier above or below the band with allowance remaining.\",\n      \"kind\": \"permission\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"For every other case, a Quality Officer can propose a decision and a Quality Manager must approve it; the proposer cannot approve their own proposal, even if they also have the Manager role.\",\n      \"kind\": \"permission\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"A decision against the system recommendation requires both the proposal and approval roles and a written justification.\",\n      \"kind\": \"permission\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"At signing, the decision-maker confirms their identity again and enters a reason; the signed decision records the decision, actor(s), reason, and signature.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"A decision cannot be signed without the required identity confirmation and reason, or without the required distinct proposer and approver.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"A signed decision cannot be edited or deleted, including by a System Administrator; a correction can only be made as a new signed decision that supersedes it, with both decisions retained.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Releasing stock returns it to its previous availability, order, and route state as applicable.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Rejecting stock removes it from its order, removes it from available stock, lists it for destruction, and causes the order to be reallocated under US-005.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Stock On Hold cannot be allocated, packed, loaded, or handed over.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"A decision still waiting more than four hours is escalated to the Quality Manager.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"A destruction record captures its date, quantity, and witness.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"The app prevents recording a destroyed quantity greater than the rejected quantity.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"readingChosen\": \"The “first tier above or below the band” means an excursion confined to an immediately adjacent tier; it qualifies for a Quality Officer acting alone only if allowance remains in every applicable tier and no non-permitted range was reached.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"US-011-lot-recall\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Only a Quality Manager can start or close a recall; each start and close action is signed.\",\n      \"kind\": \"permission\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"A Quality Manager can start a recall by selecting a product and one or more lot numbers and entering a reason and severity.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Starting a recall immediately marks all Meridian-held stock from the selected lots Recalled across every warehouse, removes it from orders, and blocks its handover, including stock packed or already on a van.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"A driver whose device is online sees “Do not deliver” for a recalled box.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"The recall trace lists every affected warehouse location, box, route, and customer delivery with quantities; the trace is available within one minute of the recall request.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"The trace exposes a quantity discrepancy if its accounted locations and deliveries do not add up exactly to the total quantity received for the lot.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"The recall identifies each customer who received the lot, with the quantities delivered, delivery dates, and receivers.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Affected customers receive an email and a customer-portal notice and can respond separately for each delivery with packs still on hand, used or dispensed, and destroyed on site.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"The app rejects a customer's reported quantity if the total reported for a delivery exceeds the quantity delivered.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Packs reported on hand are assigned to a return route and marked Quarantined when received.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"If a customer has not responded within 24 hours, the app sends a reminder and shows the outstanding customer to the Quality Manager.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Recall progress displays the percentage of packs accounted for.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"The recall accounts for packs held by Meridian, returned, reported used, reported destroyed, or written off as unaccounted.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"A recall cannot be closed while any pack is unaccounted for unless the pack has a signed write-off justification.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"readingChosen\": \"A pack reported as still on hand is collected on a return route and becomes Quarantined when it arrives at Meridian; customer quantities are accounted for per delivery.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"US-012-customer-portal\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"A customer user sees current and past orders belonging only to their own organisation; requests for another organisation's orders or deliveries are denied.\",\n      \"kind\": \"permission\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"The portal shows order status, allocated lots and expiry dates, and for a delivery on the road its planned arrival time and in-range or out-of-range temperature status.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"A customer can see only their own delivery information; the portal does not reveal other customers or their deliveries on the same route.\",\n      \"kind\": \"permission\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"For each completed delivery, the customer can download a PDF delivery certificate.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"The certificate contains products, lots, expiry dates, quantities, receiver and handover time, each box's temperature chart from sealing through handover, excursions, and their signed decisions.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Once issued, a certificate remains unchanged; if later readings alter the temperature history, the app issues a new certificate version and keeps both versions available.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"The customer can choose English or Arabic, and the portal and certificate use the selected language.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"With Arabic selected, the entire portal and certificate are right-to-left, including tables and charts.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Portal dates and times are displayed in the customer's own time zone.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"readingChosen\": \"The customer's language preference applies to the whole portal and generated certificate; Arabic uses right-to-left layout, including tables, charts, and the PDF.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"US-013-audit-trail\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Creation, change, and deletion of regulated data produces an audit entry, including changes to products and profiles, stock, orders and allocations, boxes and routes, handovers, excursions, decisions, recalls, users and roles, and configuration.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Each audit entry records who acted, when, what changed, old and new values, and any reason supplied.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Automatic actions such as system holds and allocations are recorded and attributed to the system.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"No user, including a System Administrator, can edit or delete an audit entry.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"The system provides a way to demonstrate whether the audit trail has been altered outside the application.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"An Auditor can filter audit entries by record, user, date range, and action type, and export the filtered view.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"A user can view a lot's complete history from receipt through delivery or destruction in chronological order.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Audit times use one reference time for storage and are displayed in the viewer's time zone; Karachi and Lahore use the same zone, while Dubai uses a different zone.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Audit records remain available for seven years.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     }\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"US-014-reports-summaries\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"At 07:00 in each warehouse's own time zone, the system emails that warehouse's Quality Officers a daily summary of excursions from the preceding 24 hours, decisions still waiting, silent devices, and stock On Hold.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Automatically, on the first day of each month, the system generates and emails a monthly report to configured stakeholders.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"The monthly report includes excursion counts and rates by route, driver, vehicle, and shipper-box type; rejected and destroyed packs by product and cause; on-time and in-full delivery percentages; average time from excursion to decision; stock within 60 days of expiry by product and warehouse; and open recalls with progress.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"A staff member can view report figures on screen for any date range, filter by warehouse, and export the report.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"A staff member sees report figures only for warehouses they are permitted to access.\",\n      \"kind\": \"permission\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Report figures match the underlying records for the same reporting period.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"A delivery counts as on time only if handover occurs within 60 minutes of its planned arrival, and counts as in full only if every ordered pack is handed over.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"readingChosen\": \"“Warehouse time” means each warehouse's configured local time; on-screen date-range reporting uses the same underlying record definitions as emailed summaries.\"\n   }\n  ]\n },\n {\n  \"spans\": [\n   {\n    \"id\": \"driver-route-loading-handover\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"A driver sees only routes assigned to them for today, with the route's stops in order; other drivers' routes are not visible to them.\",\n      \"kind\": \"permission\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Before departure, the driver scans the shipper boxes being loaded. Loading completes only after every box on that route has been scanned.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"A scan for a box assigned to a different route is reported as a wrong-route box and does not satisfy the expected box scan.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"When the driver attempts to finish loading with a route box unscanned, the application identifies the missing box or boxes and does not mark loading complete.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"During the route, the driver can see each box's current temperature, status and alerts.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"At a stop, the driver scans boxes for that stop. A box with On Hold stock is marked “Do not deliver,” its hold reason is shown, and the driver cannot hand it over.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"For deliverable boxes, the driver records the receiver's name, captures a signature and a photo of the delivered boxes, then completes the handover. The application records the actual handover time and location automatically.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"The driver can record a partial or full refusal by identifying each refused box and entering a reason for each; refused boxes are marked to return to the warehouse and are Quarantined when returned.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"A refusal without a reason for each refused box cannot be submitted; the driver is shown which reason is missing.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Loading scans, handovers and refusals made without a connection are retained locally with their event times and are sent automatically when a connection returns.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"An offline handover retains the time it actually occurred, rather than the later synchronization time. Sending the same handover more than once records it only once.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"When a route was changed while the driver was offline, the driver is shown the differences before continuing with the route.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"A route change or synchronization conflict does not remove or undo a handover already completed offline.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"If a hold was applied while the driver was offline after they handed over the box, the handover remains recorded, the conflicting hold is flagged, and a quality case is opened.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"When online, a driver sees “Do not deliver” for a recalled box.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"The dispatcher can see each stop's status and the time that status was last updated.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"A scan that does not identify a route box is reported as unrecognized and does not count toward loading or stop completion.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"readingChosen\": \"Treat the route, loading, delivery, refusal, offline-sync and dispatcher-status requirements as one driver workflow in the responsive web app; offline completed handovers are durable records, not provisional actions that a later route change can erase.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"US-010\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"For every affected handling unit, the reviewer sees the complete temperature history, budget used and remaining for each tier, and the system's Release or Reject recommendation.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"A Quality Officer can make and sign a sole decision when the excursion stayed within the first tier above or below the band, allowance remains, and the decision agrees with the recommendation.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"In all other cases, a Quality Officer proposes a decision and a Quality Manager approves it; the proposer cannot approve their own proposal, even if they hold both roles.\",\n      \"kind\": \"permission\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"A decision that differs from the system recommendation requires both a Quality Officer proposal and a different Quality Manager's approval, and a written justification.\",\n      \"kind\": \"permission\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Before signing, each decision-maker confirms their identity again and enters a reason.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"A decision cannot be signed when the required role, separate approver, re-confirmed identity, reason, or contrary-decision justification is missing.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"After signing, a decision cannot be edited or deleted by any user, including a System Administrator. A replacement decision is recorded as a new signed decision while the original remains available.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Stock On Hold cannot be allocated, packed, loaded or handed over.\",\n      \"kind\": \"permission\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Releasing stock removes the hold and returns it to its prior availability or, if previously assigned, to its order and route.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Rejecting stock removes it from available stock and its order, lists it for destruction, and triggers order reallocation under US-005.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"The destruction record includes a date, quantity and witness.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"The system rejects a destruction entry whose cumulative quantity would exceed the rejected quantity.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"A decision still waiting after four hours is escalated to the Quality Manager.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"readingChosen\": \"Treat the tier exception as permitting a Quality Officer to make and sign the sole decision only when the excursion remained within the first tier above or below the permitted band, allowance remains, and the decision follows the recommendation; a contrary decision always requires a proposal and approval by different people.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"US-011\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Only a Quality Manager can start or close a recall; both starting and closing require an electronic signature.\",\n      \"kind\": \"permission\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"A Quality Manager starts a recall by selecting a product and one or more lot numbers and entering a reason and severity.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Starting a recall marks all matching stock held by Meridian as Recalled across every warehouse, removes it from orders, and blocks handover, including stock already packed or on a route.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Within one minute of the request, the recall trace shows every affected warehouse location, box, route and customer delivery with quantities, and the quantities reconcile exactly to the total quantity received for the lot.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"The Quality Manager can see every customer who received the lot, including quantities, delivery dates and receivers.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Affected customers are notified by email and in the customer portal.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"A customer can respond in the portal for each delivery with packs still on hand, used or dispensed, and destroyed on site.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"A customer cannot report combined quantities greater than the quantity delivered to that customer for that delivery; the overage is rejected and the customer is shown the issue.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Packs reported on hand are collected on a return route and marked Quarantined when they arrive back.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"After 24 hours without a customer response, the customer is reminded and the Quality Manager can see that customer as outstanding.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Recall progress shows the percentage of packs accounted for.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"A recall can be closed only after every pack is accounted for as held by Meridian, returned, reported used, reported destroyed, or written off as unaccounted with a signed justification.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"The system prevents recall closure while any pack remains unaccounted for without a signed write-off.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"A driver online sees “Do not deliver” for a recalled box.\",\n      \"kind\": \"permission\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"readingChosen\": \"Treat customer accounting as per delivery and lot: customer-reported quantities are checked against that delivery, and packs reported on hand are tracked for collection and quarantine on return.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"US-012\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"A customer user sees current and past orders belonging to their own organization only; they cannot view another organization's orders or deliveries.\",\n      \"kind\": \"permission\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"For each order, the portal shows status, allocated lots and expiry dates.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"For a delivery on the road, the portal shows its planned arrival time and whether its temperature is in range or out of range, without showing other customers on the route.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"For every completed delivery, the customer can download a PDF delivery certificate showing products, lots, expiry dates, quantities, receiver and handover time, each box's temperature chart from sealing to handover, excursions, and signed decisions.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"An issued certificate remains unchanged. If late readings change the history, the system issues a new certificate version and keeps the previous version available.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"The portal and certificates are available in English or Arabic according to the user's preference; choosing Arabic 